  "live_records": {
    "q-146771": {
      "dom_id": "step-q146771",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-1)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{24}{7{x}^{4}}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=-1]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-1)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|-1}=\\frac{9}{7}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=-1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{24}{7{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{24}{7{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{7}{[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{7}[(-\\frac{1}{2})-(-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=-1] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=-1]-{\\mu }_{X|-1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{7}-{(\\frac{9}{7})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{7}-\\frac{81}{49} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{49}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
