    "q-146807": {
      "dom_id": "step-q146807",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{{x}^{3/2}}, & \\,4\\le x\\le 9 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|4}=6.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=4] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{9}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{{x}^{3/2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{9}3\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3/2}]}_{4}^{9} \\\\  & =2(27-8) \\\\  & =38.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=4]-{\\mu }_{X|4}^{2} \\\\  & =38-{6}^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
