    "q-149357": {
      "dom_id": "step-q149357",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12}{7{x}^{5/2}}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=0]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|0}=\\frac{12}{7}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=0] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{12}{7{x}^{5/2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{12}{7\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{24\\sqrt{x}}{7}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{7}-\\frac{24}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=0] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=0]-{\\mu }_{X|0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{7}-{(\\frac{12}{7})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{7}-\\frac{144}{49} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{49}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-149357-a",
