    "q-146761": {
      "dom_id": "step-q146761",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{14}\\sqrt{x}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=0]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|0}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{7}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=0] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{14}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{3}{14}{x}^{5/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{49}{x}^{7/2}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{49}(128-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{381}{49}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=0] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=0]-{\\mu }_{X|0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{381}{49}-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{7})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{381}{49}-\\frac{3}{49} \\\\  & =\\frac{378}{49} \\\\  & =\\frac{54}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
