    "q-146395": {
      "dom_id": "step-q146395",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2y, & \\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|1}=\\frac{2}{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\cdot 2y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=1]-{\\mu }_{Y|1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
