      "kp_id": "e-10340"
    },
    "q-146806": {
      "dom_id": "step-q146806",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-2)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}}, & \\,x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=-2]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-2)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|-2}=\\frac{4}{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=-2] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }4{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[4\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{-2}}{(-2)}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =0-(-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=-2] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=-2]-{\\mu }_{X|-2}^{2} \\\\  & =2-{(\\frac{4}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{16}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
