    "q-149399": {
      "dom_id": "step-q149399",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,5)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}}, & \\,x\\le -1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=5]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,5)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|5}=-\\frac{3}{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=5] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}3{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-3\\cdot {x}^{-1}]}_{-\\infty }^{-1} \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{3}{x}]}_{-\\infty }^{-1} \\\\  & =3-0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=5] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=5]-{\\mu }_{X|5}^{2} \\\\  & =3-{(-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
