    "q-149406": {
      "dom_id": "step-q149406",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-4)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{2{x}^{9/2}}, & \\,x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=-4]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-4)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|-4}=\\frac{7}{5}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=-4] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2{x}^{9/2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{7}{2{x}^{5/2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{7}{2}{x}^{-5/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{7}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{3})\\cdot {x}^{-3/2}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{7}{3{x}^{3/2}}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =0-(-\\frac{7}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=-4] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=-4]-{\\mu }_{X|-4}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}-{(\\frac{7}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}-\\frac{49}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{75}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
