    "q-149407": {
      "dom_id": "step-q149407",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,6)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{6}{{x}^{7}}, & \\,x\\le -1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=6]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,6)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|6}=-\\frac{6}{5}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=6] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}{x}^{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{6}{{x}^{7}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}-\\frac{6}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}-6{x}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{(-6)}{(-4)}\\cdot {x}^{-4}]}_{-\\infty }^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2{x}^{4}}]}_{-\\infty }^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=6] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=6]-{\\mu }_{X|6}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-{(-\\frac{6}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{36}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{50}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
