      "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF Using Improper Integrals",
      "kp_id": "e-10341"
    },
    "q-149411": {
      "dom_id": "step-q149411",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,-1)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{4{y}^{13/4}}, & \\,1\\le y \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=-1]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,-1)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|-1}=\\frac{9}{5}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=-1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{9}{4{y}^{13/4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{9}{4{y}^{5/4}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{9}{4}{y}^{-5/4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{9}{4}\\cdot (-4)\\cdot {y}^{-1/4}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{9}{\\sqrt[4]{y}}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =0-(-9) \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=-2] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=-2]-{\\mu }_{Y|-2}^{2} \\\\  & =9-{(\\frac{9}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =9-\\frac{81}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{144}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
