    "q-146981": {
      "dom_id": "step-q146981",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3({x}^{2}y+y)}{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(1+{x}^{2})}{4}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|1}=\\frac{2}{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{3({x}^{2}y+y)}{2}}{\\frac{3(1+{x}^{2})}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2({x}^{2}y+y)}{(1+{x}^{2})},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $x=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{2({1}^{2}\\cdot y+y)}{(1+{1}^{2})}=2y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}(2y)\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{3}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=1]-{\\mu }_{Y|1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
