      "source_example_id": "e-10342",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given Joint and Marginal Density Functions",
      "kp_id": "e-10342"
    },
    "q-146976": {
      "dom_id": "step-q146976",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3x(1-{y}^{2}), & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|1}=\\frac{3}{8}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x(1-{y}^{2})}{2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1-{y}^{2})}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nNotice that the factor of $x$ cancels out, leaving an expression that does not depend on $x.$ Therefore, substituting $x=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ has no effect:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{3(1-{y}^{2})}{2}\n$$\n\nThen, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3(1-{y}^{2})}{2}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-{y}^{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{5}}{5}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}[(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{5})-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=1]-{\\mu }_{Y|1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}-{(\\frac{3}{8})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}-\\frac{9}{64} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{320}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
