    "q-147052": {
      "dom_id": "step-q147052",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{1}{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{2}]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|\\frac{1}{2}}=-\\frac{7}{12}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-y}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 0.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ into the expression for ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2}-y)}{(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2})}=\\frac{1}{2}-y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{2}] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{y}^{2}(\\frac{1}{2}-y)\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{6}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{2}] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{2}]-{\\mu }_{Y|\\frac{1}{2}}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}-{(-\\frac{7}{12})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}-\\frac{49}{144} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{144}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
