    "q-146760": {
      "dom_id": "step-q146760",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(x+y)}{4}, & 0<x\\le 2y,\\,\\,0<y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}, & 0<y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=1]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|1}=\\frac{7}{6}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3(x+y)}{4})}{3{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+y}{4{y}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0<x\\le 2y,\\,0<y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=0.$ \n\nNow, substituting $y=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{x+1}{4}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=1]{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{(x+1)}{4}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{3}+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(4+\\frac{8}{3})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{20}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=1] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=1]-{\\mu }_{X|1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}-{(\\frac{7}{6})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}-\\frac{49}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
