      "source_example_id": "e-10342",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given Joint and Marginal Density Functions",
      "kp_id": "e-10342"
    },
    "q-146867": {
      "dom_id": "step-q146867",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2-x-y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}-y, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=1]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|1}=\\frac{1}{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2-x-y)}{(\\frac{3}{2}-y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-2x-2y}{3-2y},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $y=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{4-2x-2\\cdot 1}{3-2\\cdot 1}=\\frac{4-2x-2}{3-2}=2-2x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(2-2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4-3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=1] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=1]-{\\mu }_{X|1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}-{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
